        {
          "id": 803134025,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Originally, I spotted these missing headers in trace between a mail client and an imap server. I assumed that Lines: always contains a number.\n\nThe only definition of the Lines: header that I could find is related to NetNews articles, though.\n\nhttps://www.iana.org/assignments/message-headers/message-headers.xhtml\n\npoints to\n\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5536.html#section-3.3.1\n\nwhich says that only digits are allowed in the Lines: header.\n\nI guess that FT_UINT32 should be ok here.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6880719,
            "username": "martin.kaiser",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Kaiser",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/86c6c92ecb575705117c7f498cb0e8784b1ae26ca5099eafed3d9ea17626e3db?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.kaiser"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-06T12:58:58.264Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-06T12:58:58.264Z",
          "system": false,
