        {
          "id": 804714822,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thus wrote Jaap Keuter (@JaapKeuter) (gitlab@mg.gitlab.com):\n\n\n\n\n> Jaap Keuter commented on a discussion on epan/dissectors/packet-imf.c: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/5757#note_804496224\n\n> >      { &hf_imf_mailbox_list_item,\n> >        { \"Item\", \"imf.mailbox_list.item\", FT_STRING,  BASE_NONE, NULL, 0x0,\n> >          NULL, HFILL }},\n> > +    { &hf_imf_lines,\n> > +      { \"Lines\", \"imf.lines.item\", FT_UINT32,  BASE_DEC, NULL, 0x0,\n\n> But does it actually work? The code adding the item is `item = proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf_id, tvb, value_offset, end_offset - value_offset - 2, ENC_ASCII|ENC_NA);` So that's text, not a binary value in that packet, e.g. 32 != \"32\".\n\nOf course, you're right. The digits are encoded as ASCII characters.\nI'll fix my commit. Sorry for the noise.",
